are development; information processing and technology; SR and IR support; investment trust and real estate asset management; investment advising; real estate brokering; credit solution business; credit and prepaid cards; loan guarantees; agency services for credit purchases; and servicer activities. The company was formerly known as Mitsubishi Tokyo Financial Group Inc. and changed its name to Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group, Inc. in October 2005. Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group, Inc. was founded in 1880 and is headquartered in Chiyoda, Japan.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Junichi  Hanzawa | Group CEO, Group President & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 156K people. Revenue per employee of $506K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group, is a mega-cap financial services business with a $236.0B market cap on $78.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +19% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $24.4B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 74% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion 